ries a Trump endorsement, while Democrat James Byrd has raised only about $22,000 with no outside support. Every major rater calls the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats a 1-3% chance.\nThe state's R+23 partisan lean dominates the fundamentals, and no general-election polling exists to suggest otherwise. The only notable friction is criticism of Hageman for skipping PBS debates, which is unlikely to matter in a state this red. The forecast expects Hageman to win by roughly twenty points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -17.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0045, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0194, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0012, "margin": -22.0}]}